# Factory policy (cursor-agent)

This repository runs a [software factory](https://github.com/addyosmani/factory). Read
`AGENTS.md` for the project brief, then `docs/factory/CONTRACT.md` and
`docs/factory/CHARTER.md` before changing anything. For first-time setup and the local dry
run, follow `docs/factory/README.md`.

The contract is shared with Claude Code and Codex. **If this adapter and the contract
disagree, the contract wins.** Use the repo-scoped skills under `.cursor/skills/` for
factory workflows; they are thin pointers to the canonical workflows in `.claude/skills/`,
so there is one implementation, not three.

## The queue is GitHub, not this file

Live state is GitHub issue labels (`factory:*`) plus `factory-handoff:v1` issue comments.
`docs/factory/QUEUE.md` is a snapshot for humans and audit — an unmerged snapshot is never
the handoff between runs.

## The gate

```sh
./.claude/scripts/gates.sh fast   # shared-model compile + published-link check (~40s)
./.claude/scripts/gates.sh full   # + sh scripts/check-all.sh  (MINUTES — runs xcodebuild)
./.claude/scripts/gates.sh deep   # + auth surface + architecture assertions
```

Quote the final `FACTORY_GATES:` line verbatim and never report a result that contradicts
it. `RED` and `MISCONFIGURED` both block; a *required* gate that could not run is
`MISCONFIGURED`, never green.

`full` is a pre-PR gate, not a loop gate — it drives `xcodebuild` against a simulator.

## Non-negotiable

1. **Never merge**, and never push `main`. GitHub branch protection is the enforcement
   boundary.
2. **Never edit factory policy** — `docs/factory/CHARTER.md`, `.factory/gates.conf`,
   `.claude/scripts/gates.sh`, `AGENTS.md` — unless the human asks in this session.
3. **Never modify an existing `scripts/check-*`** in an unattended run. Adding a new one is
   encouraged.
4. **Verification uses a fresh context.** The writer never grades its own work. If no
   independent context is available in this harness, stop before opening anything but a
   draft PR and say so.
5. **Claim one live issue per run** by winning the deterministic remote-branch claim
   described in the contract, then move `factory:ready-to-implement` to
   `factory:in-progress`.

Stop and hand back when the charter's `STOP_IF` fires — in particular when more than two
items already await review, or when proving the change needs a physical iPhone or Watch.

## Harness gap you must compensate for by hand

Claude Code enforces the merge guard with a `PreToolUse` hook
(`.claude/hooks/block-merge.sh`, wired in `.claude/settings.json`), and Codex loads the same
script through `.codex/hooks.json`. **cursor-agent has no committed repository-hook
equivalent**, so in this harness that guard is documentation, not enforcement. Do not treat
the absence of a block as permission. The repository-side ruleset on the default branch is
the only real boundary in every harness.
